# References / inspiration (default — never remove)

When the user gives something to copy or follow (screenshot, link, another repo, competitor app, old project, design file):

## Take

- Only the parts that are **actually needed** for the requested surface or feature
- Structure, layout, flow, spacing rhythm, interaction pattern, field order
- Re-express everything using **this project's** tokens, components, naming, and concept

## Do not carry over

- The source's name, brand, logo, trademark, product wording, or marketing copy
- Source URLs, file paths, repo names, or screenshots referenced in code or docs
- Comments, commit messages, PR text, docs, or UI copy that say where it came from
  (no "inspired by X", "same as Y", "ported from Z", "based on the reference")
- Class names, variable names, or CSS custom properties that leak the source
- Unused sections, dead options, or extra pages that came along with the reference

## Treat the output as fresh

- The project must read as if it was authored **only for this project**
- Adapt names to the project concept (`concept-domain.mdc`) and tokens (`frontend-design`)
- Defaults still apply: unified custom forms, project styling, validation, PHP migrate/seed
- If the reference conflicts with a default rule or the concept, the **project wins** — say so and adapt

## In chat vs in files

- In chat, you may say what you took and how you adapted it
- In **files** (code, comments, docs, README, commits), leave no trace of the source
